From 442c29aa044ae43b444f67c3ab28583fec2199c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Beany <24502088+beanyforever@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:46:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The attribute caches keep the attributes put last, however
 close the puts

SiYuan keeps blocks' and documents' attributes in two ristretto caches.
ristretto takes in a key it doesn't hold yet later, on its own goroutine, and
turns away a second put of that key queued before the first is taken in, as
one it already holds. So when two puts of a new key came close together, the
cache kept the first.

"+ New" in a database does this to the page it makes. Inserting the row,
fillDefaultValue renders the view to find the row next to it
(getAttrViewAddingBlockDefaultValues, getNearItem), which reads the new page's
attributes from its file and puts them in the cache (BatchGetBlockAttrs,
getBlockAttrsFromTree), before the page is bound. A fraction of a millisecond
later, bindBlockAv0 binds it and puts its attributes again, with custom-avs
(setNodeAttrsWithTx). About 1 time in 3 to 6 the second put was turned away,
and the cache kept the page's attributes without custom-avs until SiYuan
restarted or they were put again. /api/attr/getBlockAttrs then lacked
custom-avs, and /api/av/getAttributeViewKeys, which starts from it, listed no
database for the page, though the database, the page's file and SQL all held
the binding.

A put to either cache now returns once the cache holds its attributes, and
puts to one cache take turns, so a read after a put gives what was put.
SiYuan's tree and database caches already guard against the same ristretto
behaviour, with a generation per key.
---
 kernel/cache/ial.go             |  4 +--
 kernel/cache/ial_latest.go      | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 kernel/cache/ial_latest_test.go | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 kernel/cache/ial_latest.go
 create mode 100644 kernel/cache/ial_latest_test.go

diff --git a/kernel/cache/ial.go b/kernel/cache/ial.go
index de41b2f..76d5b4e 100644
--- a/kernel/cache/ial.go
+++ b/kernel/cache/ial.go
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ func PutDocIALInBox(p, boxID string, ial map[string]string) {
 		RemoveDocIALInBox(p, boxID)
 		return
 	}
-	docIALCache.Set(key, maps.Clone(ial), cost)
+	putLatestIAL(docIALCache, &docIALPutMu, key, maps.Clone(ial), cost)
 
 	docIALCacheKeysMu.Lock()
 	defer docIALCacheKeysMu.Unlock()
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ func PutBlockIALInBox(id, boxID string, ial map[string]string) {
 		RemoveBlockIALInBox(id, boxID)
 		return
 	}
-	blockIALCache.Set(key, maps.Clone(ial), cost)
+	putLatestIAL(blockIALCache, &blockIALPutMu, key, maps.Clone(ial), cost)
 
 	blockIALCacheKeysMu.Lock()
 	defer blockIALCacheKeysMu.Unlock()
